        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "02b4a95c-dcb4-379f-8d63-1752945a032c",
                "word": "inexorablement",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "44ff1da8-b14f-389a-a9d7-990e5b7ffd32",
                        "entry_id": "02b4a95c-dcb4-379f-8d63-1752945a032c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "D’une manière inexorable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "39524964-f475-4163-bf4b-32fe1c19b772",
                                "sense_id": "44ff1da8-b14f-389a-a9d7-990e5b7ffd32",
                                "text": "Pendant ce temps, ma mutation morphologique se poursuit, inexorablement. En plus de mes jambes atrophiées, d’autres signes conjecturés semblent devoir se confirmer, des petits pieds et de petites mains, un crâne disproportionné, des traits assez grossiers avec un menton fuyant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4247d762-e984-452d-bff8-45ee451d4817",
                                "sense_id": "44ff1da8-b14f-389a-a9d7-990e5b7ffd32",
                                "text": "C'est là le juste supplice du pécheur qui se retire de Dieu, que Dieu aussi se retire de lui, et par cette soustraction le prive de tout le bien et l’investisse irremédiablement et inexorablement de tout le mal."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab4b94cb-3849-4c9d-bbac-fae2d214e896",
                                "sense_id": "44ff1da8-b14f-389a-a9d7-990e5b7ffd32",
                                "text": "Elle avait un sari tellement usé que le bleu d'origine tirait inexorablement vers le blanc."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "64a85531-d4cd-4836-9589-b867bf2c6eab",
                        "source_entry_id": "02b4a95c-dcb4-379f-8d63-1752945a032c",
                        "source_sense_id": "44ff1da8-b14f-389a-a9d7-990e5b7ffd32",
                        "target_lang_word": "inexorably",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inexorably",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "94fa19f5-c685-3c6a-9d8f-ee0eba367f65",
                                        "entry_id": "9c50a835-6198-337a-b4da-964534d3e9ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an inexorable manner; without the possibility of stopping or prevention."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12df2b66-037d-4849-b8ce-4c6968829bb4",
                                                "sense_id": "94fa19f5-c685-3c6a-9d8f-ee0eba367f65",
                                                "text": "Later, they all felt guilty about having laughed, especially when it looked as if she might not be able to walk again. But she did, eventually—implacably, inexorably—with a slight limp, perhaps, although this was barely noticeable, not noticeable at all, really, unless you knew the story, unless you were watching for it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "feacf331-d848-4751-b83b-e1ef188ef7e9",
                                                "sense_id": "94fa19f5-c685-3c6a-9d8f-ee0eba367f65",
                                                "text": "We watched as the storm clouds advanced inexorably closer to us."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddb09b8e-7ef6-45db-9abd-50eb25d089fd",
                                                "sense_id": "94fa19f5-c685-3c6a-9d8f-ee0eba367f65",
                                                "text": "One of his best stories was \"Barney Oldfield's Race for a Life\" (1914), of which there survives only an amusing still, showing poor Mabel Normand chained to the rails by two toughs, the moustached villain threatening her with a sledge-hammer, and an awful sense of that inexorably approaching express!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa1eff79-6583-4bba-b9f5-7a294cc042c0",
                                                "sense_id": "94fa19f5-c685-3c6a-9d8f-ee0eba367f65",
                                                "text": "The strange group of villagers shuffled inexorably forward."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e347c3a-078f-41ba-80eb-c596a7e73227",
                                                "sense_id": "94fa19f5-c685-3c6a-9d8f-ee0eba367f65",
                                                "text": "While it remains a burden assiduously avoided, it is not unexpected, and thus not beyond a measure of control. Which has led you, inexorably, here."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a162e212-7d05-4608-b3d8-b4ef72e76eb4",
                                                "sense_id": "94fa19f5-c685-3c6a-9d8f-ee0eba367f65",
                                                "text": "The fact that the juggernaut of Indian English rolls inexorably on, largely unconcerned by the academic arguments taking place about it, is in itself an indicator of an endonormative force in the variety, and this can be traced historically."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a238fa48-4dd2-46ff-8464-993286538019",
                                                "sense_id": "94fa19f5-c685-3c6a-9d8f-ee0eba367f65",
                                                "text": "This magnificent picture really stopped me in my tracks when I stumbled across it. I was drawn inexorably and immediately into the compelling detail discernible on this top-quality image."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b2a9da1-7cdb-465c-b773-207ebbbc92cb",
                                                "sense_id": "94fa19f5-c685-3c6a-9d8f-ee0eba367f65",
                                                "text": "The creative commons of the internet has been gradually and inexorably enclosed, much as agricultural land was by parliamentary acts from 1600 onwards in England."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5bfeea8e-c735-4b27-a9bf-04a30138ed42",
                        "source_entry_id": "02b4a95c-dcb4-379f-8d63-1752945a032c",
                        "source_sense_id": "44ff1da8-b14f-389a-a9d7-990e5b7ffd32",
                        "target_lang_word": "inexorablemente",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inexorablemente",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "25ca45ea-704c-392e-9c80-4ffba11a8b1b",
                                        "entry_id": "b05d484b-6468-32b6-8706-c36ba3ae347a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Inevitablemente."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbfe9260-0ef1-4766-8933-dbf1d1c760c8",
                                                "sense_id": "25ca45ea-704c-392e-9c80-4ffba11a8b1b",
                                                "text": "Se sintió inmensamente triste cuando pensó en la imagen de sus padres, sonriendo, como una figura que cada vez se iba alejando de más y más de ella. No, en realidad era ella quien se alejaba cada vez más de ellos, de su recuerdo. Seguramente se iría acostumbrando cada día más a estar sin sus padres, lo que le producía una inmensa tristeza. Fue precisamente para evitar esto que, después del accidente, Bianca se había encargado de convertir su nueva habitación en una especie de santuario personal con el fin de siempre tener presentes a sus padres, por más de que pasara el tiempo. Para esto, había mandado a imprimir varias fotos de ellos y las había colocado en cuadros, en varios lugares de su habitación. En el protector de la pantalla de su celular y de la laptop que le habían regalado sus tíos. Sin embargo, a medida que iban pasando los días, Bianca entendía que sus padres se iban quedando, inexorablemente, cada vez más y más atrás. De hecho, ella los iba dejando con cada nuevo día que pasaba en este mundo»."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "857b4ce3-9e0e-30aa-b74f-f9903fa5063d",
                                        "entry_id": "b05d484b-6468-32b6-8706-c36ba3ae347a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Propio de las personas inexorables."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "612525e1-11bc-40c7-a84e-d6b91de0ff35",
                        "source_entry_id": "02b4a95c-dcb4-379f-8d63-1752945a032c",
                        "source_sense_id": "44ff1da8-b14f-389a-a9d7-990e5b7ffd32",
